===== path share
Share an agent session to Pathbase via an interactive picker

Usage: path share [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --url <URL>
          Pathbase server URL (defaults to the stored session's server)

      --anon
          Force the anonymous endpoint, ignoring any stored credentials

      --repo <REPO>
          Target a specific repo as `owner/name` instead of `<you>/pathstash`

      --name <NAME>
          Human-readable display label for the uploaded graph (defaults to the toolpath document id). Free-form; not used in the URL — graphs are addressed by UUID server-side

      --public
          Mark the uploaded graph public (default: unlisted, addressable only by UUID)

      --harness <HARNESS>
          Narrow the picker to one harness, or skip the picker entirely when used with --session
          
          [possible values: claude, gemini, codex, opencode, cursor, cursor-agent, pi, copilot]

      --session <SESSION>
          Skip the picker. Requires --harness; requires --project for claude/gemini/pi

      --project <PROJECT>
          Override cwd-as-project. Filters the picker to sessions tied to this project across all harnesses

      --no-cache
          Skip writing the cache; derive in-memory only

      --timeout <SECS>
          Seconds to allow the upload before giving up (default 300).
          
          A long session derives to several MB and goes up in one request, so the ceiling that suits every other call is the wrong one here. Sets `PATH_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECS` for this invocation; export that directly for commands that have no flag, or for an agent that runs `share` for you.

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
